  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;be a conic. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> be the focus and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> be the point on the axis of the conic such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8869;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is any point on the conic. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is the ordinate of the centroid of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
